{"id":"sat-evidence-inference","title":"SAT Reading and Writing: evidence and inference","subject":"English","label":"SAT","exams":["sat"],"language":"en","seconds":169,"duration":169.37,"audio":"voice.mp3","words":479,"sections":[{"id":"hook","title":"The puzzle","start":0,"end":15.445},{"id":"explain","title":"Core idea","start":15.445,"end":49.505},{"id":"explain2","title":"Choices","start":49.505,"end":74.245},{"id":"example","title":"Worked example","start":74.245,"end":103.725},{"id":"check","title":"Quick check","start":103.725,"end":115.105},{"id":"answer","title":"Answer","start":115.105,"end":129.935},{"id":"mistakes","title":"Mistakes","start":129.935,"end":150.745},{"id":"recap","title":"Recap","start":150.745,"end":169.37}],"lines":[{"s":0,"a":0.5,"b":7.07,"text":"Imagine two answers both sound true. One fits the passage. One only fits your own experience.","w":[0.58,1.08,1.44,1.92,2.28,2.62,3.56,3.8,4.08,4.2,5.14,5.38,5.64,5.88,6.14,6.32]},{"s":0,"a":7.37,"b":15.02,"text":"How do you choose? I'm Kora, and this is how the SAT tests evidence and inference. It is simpler than it looks.","w":[7.42,7.56,7.68,7.82,8.66,8.86,9.68,9.8,10.02,10.12,10.28,10.62,11.28,11.76,12.36,12.54,13.62,13.74,13.88,14.32,14.5,14.58]},{"s":1,"a":15.87,"b":19.56,"text":"An inference is a conclusion the passage makes almost certain.","w":[15.96,16.14,16.68,16.8,16.88,17.8,17.94,18.4,18.72,19.16]},{"s":1,"a":19.86,"b":22.62,"text":"It is not a guess, and it is not outside knowledge.","w":[19.92,20.02,20.16,20.34,20.44,21.02,21.14,21.26,21.38,21.68,22.1]},{"s":1,"a":22.92,"b":25.87,"text":"The right answer must be supported by words in the text.","w":[22.94,23.1,23.4,23.74,23.98,24.12,24.6,24.82,25.28,25.38,25.48]},{"s":1,"a":26.17,"b":30.08,"text":"On the digital SAT, every question has its own short passage.","w":[26.24,26.34,26.44,27.04,28.2,28.46,28.9,29.08,29.28,29.46,29.72]},{"s":1,"a":30.38,"b":33.18,"text":"The passage is short, so every sentence matters.","w":[30.4,30.54,30.98,31.1,31.8,32.06,32.32,32.72]},{"s":1,"a":33.48,"b":36.23,"text":"You do not need outside facts, even if you know them.","w":[33.52,33.66,33.8,34.02,34.34,34.76,35.42,35.62,35.72,35.84,36.04]},{"s":1,"a":36.53,"b":42.05,"text":"Evidence questions ask which choice most strongly supports a claim or most logically completes it.","w":[36.6,36.98,37.6,38.02,38.3,38.72,39,39.44,39.84,39.9,40.54,40.7,41,41.48,41.9]},{"s":1,"a":42.35,"b":45.47,"text":"Read the question first, then find the exact claim.","w":[42.42,42.64,42.78,43.24,44.04,44.3,44.58,44.72,45.2]},{"s":1,"a":45.77,"b":49.08,"text":"Predict the answer in your own words before you look at the choices.","w":[45.78,46.14,46.38,46.78,46.86,47.1,47.3,47.68,47.94,48.08,48.26,48.34,48.48]},{"s":2,"a":49.93,"b":55.35,"text":"Now, the choices. Wrong answers often sound smart, but they fail in predictable ways.","w":[50.02,50.68,50.84,51.72,52.12,52.5,52.78,53.08,53.76,53.88,54.06,54.32,54.42,54.94]},{"s":2,"a":55.65,"b":58.81,"text":"Some are too extreme, with words like always or never.","w":[55.74,55.98,56.16,56.38,57.18,57.38,57.7,58.02,58.38,58.48]},{"s":2,"a":59.11,"b":61.61,"text":"Some are true in life but not in the passage.","w":[59.26,59.48,59.64,59.92,60.06,60.46,60.64,60.86,60.94,61.06]},{"s":2,"a":61.91,"b":65.84,"text":"Some are only half right, so one detail fits and another does not.","w":[62,62.2,62.34,62.58,62.86,63.64,63.9,64.06,64.5,64.86,65,65.3,65.5]},{"s":2,"a":66.14,"b":70.07,"text":"That is why every part of the choice must be backed by words in the passage.","w":[66.16,66.4,66.52,66.92,67.16,67.38,67.48,67.6,68.04,68.3,68.48,68.84,69.04,69.34,69.44,69.54]},{"s":2,"a":70.37,"b":73.82,"text":"If you cannot point to the words that prove it, it is not the answer.","w":[70.44,70.56,70.74,71.1,71.36,71.48,71.58,71.84,72.02,72.3,72.8,72.92,73.08,73.3,73.48]},{"s":3,"a":74.67,"b":81.29,"text":"Here is a tiny passage. After the city added bike lanes, the number of cyclists doubled, but car traffic stayed the same.","w":[74.72,74.96,75.1,75.18,75.52,76.5,76.74,76.88,77.18,77.42,77.66,78.24,78.38,78.62,78.72,79.18,79.76,79.96,80.22,80.6,80.84,80.96]},{"s":3,"a":81.59,"b":86.31,"text":"Which inference is supported? The new cyclists were mostly not former drivers.","w":[81.62,81.94,82.42,82.52,83.5,83.68,83.92,84.58,84.78,85.24,85.46,85.76]},{"s":3,"a":86.61,"b":90.38,"text":"Not that bike lanes reduce traffic, because car traffic did not change.","w":[86.68,86.92,87.12,87.4,87.7,88.04,88.76,89.1,89.34,89.72,89.88,90.08]},{"s":3,"a":90.68,"b":96.01,"text":"So where did the new riders come from? Not from behind the wheel, or car traffic would have dropped.","w":[90.78,91.04,91.26,91.38,91.52,91.72,92.1,92.3,93.2,93.44,93.6,93.9,94,94.54,94.7,94.96,95.32,95.46,95.56]},{"s":3,"a":96.31,"b":99.65,"text":"You can point to doubled cyclists and unchanged car traffic.","w":[96.32,96.46,96.66,96.94,97.12,97.5,98.22,98.44,99.02,99.26]},{"s":3,"a":99.95,"b":103.3,"text":"The passage supports the first inference, not the second.","w":[99.96,100.14,100.64,101.14,101.34,101.68,102.58,102.78,102.92]},{"s":4,"a":104.15,"b":108.32,"text":"Quick check. A plant grew taller only in the pots that got morning sun.","w":[104.2,104.46,105.4,105.5,105.82,106.08,106.58,106.8,106.88,107,107.32,107.46,107.66,108]},{"s":4,"a":108.62,"b":112.45,"text":"What can you infer? Think about what the words actually say.","w":[108.7,108.94,109.12,109.3,110.42,110.68,110.94,111.12,111.24,111.66,112.14]},{"s":4,"a":112.75,"b":114.68,"text":"Pause here and try it. I'll wait.","w":[112.76,113.08,113.32,113.44,113.72,114.18,114.34]},{"s":5,"a":115.53,"b":119.49,"text":"Morning sun helped that plant grow, because only the sunny pots improved.","w":[115.6,115.96,116.22,116.54,116.74,117.08,117.68,118.06,118.3,118.44,118.72,119.02]},{"s":5,"a":119.79,"b":122.49,"text":"You cannot infer that all plants need morning sun.","w":[119.8,119.98,120.36,120.74,121,121.2,121.6,121.82,122.18]},{"s":5,"a":122.79,"b":126.12,"text":"The proof is the phrase only in the pots that got morning sun.","w":[122.82,122.98,123.38,123.5,123.64,124.16,124.4,124.5,124.62,124.98,125.16,125.42,125.8]},{"s":5,"a":126.42,"b":129.51,"text":"That is your evidence, right there in the text.","w":[126.48,126.8,126.92,127.16,128.1,128.36,128.92,129.02,129.12]},{"s":6,"a":130.36,"b":136.77,"text":"One mistake is choosing an answer that is true in life but absent from the passage. Check the text for proof.","w":[130.5,130.66,131.24,131.4,131.76,131.88,132.28,132.46,132.64,132.94,133.06,133.54,133.84,134.22,134.38,134.5,135.6,135.84,135.96,136.32,136.5]},{"s":6,"a":137.07,"b":142.99,"text":"Another is accepting extreme wording like always or never. Prefer the careful claim the passage supports.","w":[137.14,137.62,137.76,138.24,138.76,139.16,139.5,139.88,139.98,140.58,141,141.14,141.58,141.9,142.02,142.46]},{"s":6,"a":143.29,"b":147.69,"text":"A third is stopping at half right. Make sure every part of the choice fits.","w":[143.34,143.5,143.9,144.02,144.48,144.64,144.94,145.7,145.94,146.24,146.46,146.7,146.78,146.9,147.22]},{"s":6,"a":147.99,"b":150.32,"text":"Ask yourself, where is my proof?","w":[148.1,148.32,149.32,149.58,149.7,149.88]},{"s":7,"a":151.17,"b":154.2,"text":"Recap. Inference means almost certain from the text.","w":[151.22,152,152.44,152.84,153.2,153.52,153.68,153.8]},{"s":7,"a":154.5,"b":156.83,"text":"Evidence choices need words you can point to.","w":[154.6,154.98,155.44,155.68,156.02,156.14,156.3,156.56]},{"s":7,"a":157.13,"b":160.68,"text":"Predict first, then match, and reject extremes.","w":[157.18,157.62,158.42,158.72,159.36,159.5,159.98]},{"s":7,"a":160.98,"b":164.58,"text":"Exam tip: if you cannot underline the proof, do not choose it.","w":[161.08,161.48,161.92,162.02,162.14,162.56,163,163.1,163.8,163.96,164.2,164.5]},{"s":7,"a":164.88,"b":168.77,"text":"Keep practicing with Knowzone, and you will make these questions feel simple.","w":[164.9,165.16,165.7,165.86,166.84,166.96,167.08,167.26,167.44,167.66,168.14,168.42]}],"scenes":[{"at":0.25,"heading":"Two answers","items":[{"at":0.4,"kind":"text","text":"Two answers sound true: one fits text, one fits you"},{"at":7.27,"kind":"text","text":"SAT evidence/inference is simpler than it looks"}]},{"at":15.62,"heading":"Core idea","items":[{"at":15.77,"kind":"term","text":"Inference","detail":"Conclusion the passage makes almost certain"},{"at":19.76,"kind":"text","text":"Not a guess; not outside knowledge"},{"at":22.82,"kind":"text","text":"Right answer: supported by words in text"},{"at":26.07,"kind":"text","text":"Digital SAT: each question has a short passage"},{"at":33.38,"kind":"text","text":"No outside facts needed, even if you know them"}]},{"at":36.28,"heading":"Evidence questions","items":[{"at":36.43,"kind":"text","text":"Ask: which choice most strongly supports/completes?"},{"at":42.25,"kind":"text","text":"Read question first; find exact claim"},{"at":45.67,"kind":"text","text":"Predict answer in your own words first"}]},{"at":49.68,"heading":"Wrong choices","items":[{"at":55.55,"kind":"text","text":"Too extreme: always, never"},{"at":59.01,"kind":"text","text":"True in life, not in passage"},{"at":61.81,"kind":"text","text":"Half right: one detail fits, one does not"},{"at":66.04,"kind":"text","text":"Every part of the choice needs proof in the text"},{"at":70.27,"kind":"text","text":"No proof words? Not the answer"}]},{"at":74.42,"heading":"Worked example","items":[{"at":74.57,"kind":"text","text":"Bike lanes → cyclists doubled; car traffic same"},{"at":81.49,"kind":"text","text":"Supported: new cyclists mostly not former drivers"},{"at":86.51,"kind":"text","text":"Not: bike lanes reduce traffic (car traffic same)"},{"at":90.58,"kind":"text","text":"If drivers had switched, car traffic would drop"},{"at":96.21,"kind":"text","text":"Proof: cyclists doubled + car traffic unchanged"}]},{"at":103.72,"heading":"Quick check","items":[{"at":103.72,"kind":"question","text":"A plant grew taller only in the pots that got morning sun. What can you infer?"}]},{"at":115.28,"heading":"Answer","items":[{"at":115.43,"kind":"text","text":"Morning sun helped that plant grow"},{"at":119.69,"kind":"text","text":"Cannot infer all plants need morning sun"},{"at":122.69,"kind":"text","text":"Proof: 'only in the pots that got morning sun'"},{"at":126.32,"kind":"text","text":"Evidence is in the text"}]},{"at":130.11,"heading":"Mistakes","items":[{"at":130.26,"kind":"wrong","text":"True in life but absent from passage"},{"at":136.97,"kind":"wrong","text":"Extreme wording: always, never"},{"at":143.19,"kind":"wrong","text":"Stopping at half right"},{"at":147.89,"kind":"tip","text":"Ask yourself: where is my proof?"}]},{"at":150.92,"heading":"Recap","items":[{"at":151.07,"kind":"text","text":"Inference = almost certain from text"},{"at":154.4,"kind":"text","text":"Evidence choices need words you can point to"},{"at":157.03,"kind":"text","text":"Predict → match → reject extremes"},{"at":160.88,"kind":"tip","text":"If you cannot underline the proof, do not choose it."},{"at":164.78,"kind":"text","text":"Practice with Knowzone"}]}],"check":{"at":114.93,"seconds":10,"question":"A plant grew taller only in the pots that got morning sun. What can you infer?","answer":"Morning sun helped that plant grow; only sunny pots improved. Not all plants need morning sun."},"fps":30,"mouth":"","level":"","credits":[],"voice":"qwen3-tts-12hz-1.7b (cloned voice)"}